<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore Nov 14-20 weekly oil product stocks down.</title>
<headline>Singapore Nov 14-20 weekly oil product stocks down.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore weekly residue stocks fell by 148,000 barrels in the week ended November 20 to 10.959 million barrels, Singapore's Trade Development Board (TDB) said.</p>
<p>They include HSFO, LSFO, LSWR and the straight-run atmospheric residue, but exclude bitumen.</p>
<p>Middle-distillate stocks also fell by 652,000 barrels to 8.366 million barrels. Middle distillates comprise jet, kerosene and gas oil.  </p>
<p>Light distillate stocks were down by 219,000 barrels to 5.160 million barrels. They comprise gasoline, reformate and naphtha.</p>
<p>TDB had earlier released figures which repeated the data for the previous week ending November 13.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-870-3082)</p>
</text>
